<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Engke Temür</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1405</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Engke Temür was a Chagatayid prince of Kara Del, the Mongol principality centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hami">Hami</a> in the eastern Tarim region. In 1404 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a> recognised him as Prince of Zhongshun, and soon afterwards it set up the Hami Guard, making the oasis a Ming frontier client on the route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p></div>
